// Title: Outlook Macro Execution Without Warning Setting Enabled
// Sigma ID: e3b50fa5-3c3f-444e-937b-0a99d33731cd
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: @ScoubiMtl
// Date: 2021-04-05 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, command-and-control, T1137, T1008, T1546
// Description: Detects the modification of Outlook security setting to allow unprompted execution of macros.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.mdsec.co.uk/2020/11/a-fresh-outlook-on-mail-based-persistence/
//   - https://speakerdeck.com/heirhabarov/hunting-for-persistence-via-microsoft-exchange-server-or-outlook?slide=53
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_office_outlook_enable_macro_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Outlook\\Security\\Level" and RegistryValueData contains "0x00000001"
